invariant: INV-17
file: ghash_hw.c
catches: ghash_equiv_test
reason: the host object's GHASH data loop wipes its state only up to the powers
  of the hash subkey, so H * x^-1 to H^8 * x^-1 stay in the dead frame
  after every call, and a later caller's uninitialized stack reads them.
  Each is a function of the key, and the first is the subkey shifted by
  one bit. No output changes, so no vector notices. bin/ghash_equiv_test
  copies the stack below one call over three passes and requires no power
  of H in the copy.

--- old
    ct_wipe(&s, offsetof(ghash_state, powers) + powers * sizeof s.powers[0]);
--- new
    ct_wipe(&s, offsetof(ghash_state, powers));
